- [will_said] KIT PLATFORMS + WPM RULINGS (Will, 2026-11-17 ~06:40-06:54 CST): the kit ships builds for Windows, Linux, Mac, iOS, and Android (15-cell matrix with the three editions). The kit includes a package manager for C; Conan and vcpkg were evaluated on contents and neither fits, so under Will's conditional (if there is not a great one, build it too) it is built in-programme and named by Will: wpm, Will's Package Manager. wpm is distributed - no central registry, anyone can host a node; package identity is hash-pinned (SHA-256) and publisher-signed, nodes are untrusted carriers; a node can host any GitHub repo + tag and other popular C sites, and the hash pinned at resolution is the identity since upstream tags can move.

